## User question:
Add the route 192.168.10.0/24 to the BGP routing table on a Nokia router without allowing recursion to tunnels.
---
## Proposed answer:
route-distinguisher auto
vrf definition default-vrf
rd auto
import default-vrf
export default-vrf
address-family ipv4 unicast
network 192.168.10.0 mask 255.255.255.0
redistribute connected
exit-address-family
router bgp 65000
vrf default
neighbor 192.168.10.1 remote-as 65000
neighbor 192.168.10.1 route-map NO_TUNNEL out
route-map NO_TUNNEL permit 10
match ip address prefix-list NO_TUNNEL
exit
ip prefix-list NO_TUNNEL seq 10 permit 192.168.10.0/24
exit
---
