## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to prevent repeated BGP session flapping when the interface used for EBGP connections frequently alternates between Up and Down states?
---
## Proposed answer:
set protocols bgp group <group-name> type external
set protocols bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip>
set protocols bgp group <group-name> down-stream-ebgp-relax
set protocols bgp group <group-name> soft-reconfiguration inbound
set protocols bgp group <group-name> timers keepalive 30 hold 90
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
ebgp-interface-sensitive
undo ebgp-interface-sensitive
FuncDef:
The ebgp-interface-sensitive command immediately resets BGP sessions between the local interface and directly connected EBGP peers if the local interface goes Down.
The undo ebgp-interface-sensitive command disables the function.
By default, this function is enabled.
