"How to configure Nokia router's BGP VPNv4 peer group 'VPN_GROUP' to both send and receive Add-Path routes?"
---
## Proposed answer:
peer-group VPN_GROUP
send-add-path
receive-add-path
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <group-name> capability-advertise add-path { both | receive | send }
undo peer <group-name> capability-advertise add-path { both | receive | send }
FuncDef:
The peer capability-advertise add-path command enables BGP Add-Path function.
The undo peer capability-advertise add-path command restores the default setting.
By default, the route-refresh and 4-byte AS number functions are enabled, but the general router function and Add-Path are disabled.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'group-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of a peer group.\nThe name is a string of 1 to 47 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
{'Parameters': 'add-path', 'Info': 'Indicates the Add-Path function.\nadd-path takes effect only on IBGP peers.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'both', 'Info': 'Enables the RR to receive Add-Path routes from and send Add-Path routes to a specified IBGP peer.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'receive', 'Info': 'Enables the RR to receive Add-Path routes from a specified IBGP peer.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'send', 'Info': 'Enables the RR to send Add-Path routes to a specified IBGP peer.\n-'}
