How to configure Nokia router to filter outgoing BGP routes advertised to peer 192.168.50.20 using AS_Path filter named "CUSTOM_FILTER"?
---
## Proposed answer:
filter-policies CUSTOM_FILTER out peer 192.168.50.20
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <ipv4-address> as-path-filter { <number> | <name> } export
undo peer <ipv4-address> as-path-filter { <number> | <name> } export
FuncDef:
The peer as-path-filter export command configures a policy based on an AS_Path list for filtering BGP routes to be advertised to a specified peer.
The undo peer as-path-filter export command cancels this configuration.
By default, no policy based on an AS_Path list is configured for filtering BGP routes to be advertised to a peer, and all the BGP routes will be advertised to the peer.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv4-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv4 address of a peer.\nIt is in dotted decimal notation.'}
{'Parameters': 'number', 'Info': 'Specifies the number of an AS_Path filter.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 1 to 256.'}
{'Parameters': 'name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of an AS_Path filter.\nThe value is a string of 1 to 51 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
---
