## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to establish a BGP VPNv6 peer relationship with 2001:DB8:2::2 using fake AS number 65001 while allowing both actual and fake AS numbers, and prepending the fake AS to received routes?
---
## Proposed answer:
router bgp 65001
address-family ipv6 vpn
neighbor 2001:DB8:2::2 remote-as 65001
neighbor 2001:DB8:2::2 allow-as-fake
neighbor 2001:DB8:2::2 as-override
neighbor 2001:DB8:2::2 route-map PREPEND_FAKE_AS in
exit-address-family
---
