---
## Proposed answer:
set routing-instances default protocols static route 0.0.0.0/0 next-hop <outbound-interface> popgo
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
unicast-route label advertise
unicast-route label advertise pop-go
undo unicast-route label advertise
undo unicast-route label advertise pop-go
FuncDef:
The unicast-route label advertise command enables a device to convert received IPv4 public network unicast routes to labeled routes by allocating one BGP label to each route and advertise the labeled routes to peers with the labeled route exchange capability.
The undo unicast-route label advertise command restores the default configuration.
The unicast-route label advertise pop-go command enables a device to convert received IPv4 public network unicast routes to labeled routes by adding a BGP label to each route and advertise the labeled routes to peers with the labeled route exchange capability. If the IP address of an outbound interface is reachable but no LSP is reachable, traffic is forwarded through the outbound interface and a specific next hop, during which the label POPGO action is performed.
The undo unicast-route label advertise pop-go command restores the default configuration.
By default, a device does not convert received IPv4 public network unicast routes to labeled routes.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
