## User question:
How to configure Nokia router to set priority values of 150 for EBGP routes, 180 for IBGP routes, and 220 for local routes in BGP-VPN IPv6 address family?
---
## Proposed answer:
router bgp <AS_NUMBER>
address-family ipv6 vrf <VRF_NAME>
default-metric 0
autonomous-system <AS_NUMBER>
redistribute connected metric 220 route-map LOCAL_PRIORITY
route-map LOCAL_PRIORITY permit 10
match ip address prefix-list LOCAL
set metric 220
!
redistribute bgp <NEIGHBOR_AS> metric 180 route-map IBGP_PRIORITY
route-map IBGP_PRIORITY permit 10
match ip address prefix-list IBGP
set metric 180
!
redistribute bgp <NEIGHBOR_AS> metric 150 route-map EBGP_PRIORITY
route-map EBGP_PRIORITY permit 10
match ip address prefix-list EBGP
set metric 150
!
---
